Subject: [PATCH] Use RGBA SHM readback when GLES cannot read BGRA

Mali-400 MP (GLES 2.0, EGL Linux-r6p1-01rel0) supports BGRA textures
but not GL_EXT_read_format_bgra. The unconditional BGRA glReadPixels
fails with GL_INVALID_ENUM, leaving the shared-memory page frame empty.

Keep BGRA reads on desktop GL and GLES with the read-format extension.
Otherwise read RGBA/UNSIGNED_BYTE and swap R/B in the owned SHM bitmap.
This only changes the SHM target; direct presentation is unaffected.

Device evidence: RGBA FBO probe passed; BGRA returned 0x500. Applying
the equivalent conversion via a temporary dispatch shim restored page
rendering in the installed app. This native patch has not yet been
validated in a full rebuilt WebKit on the TV.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #include <array>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+#include <utility>
 #include <wtf/SafeStrerror.h>
 #include <wtf/SystemTracing.h>
 #include <wtf/TZoneMallocInlines.h>
@@ -513,7 +514,19 @@ AcceleratedSurface::RenderTargetSHMImage::~RenderTargetSHMImage()
 
 void AcceleratedSurface::RenderTargetSHMImage::didRenderFrame(Vector<IntRect, 1>&& damageRects)
 {
-    glReadPixels(0, 0, m_bitmap->size().width(), m_bitmap->size().height(), GL_BGRA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, m_bitmap->mutableSpan().data());
+    bool supportsBGRAReadback = true;
+#if USE(LIBEPOXY)
+    // BGRA texture support does not imply BGRA readback support on GLES.
+    supportsBGRAReadback = epoxy_is_desktop_gl() || epoxy_has_gl_extension("GL_EXT_read_format_bgra");
+#endif
+    ASSERT(m_bitmap->bytesPerRow() == static_cast<size_t>(m_bitmap->size().width()) * 4);
+    auto pixels = m_bitmap->mutableSpan().first(m_bitmap->sizeInBytes());
+    glReadPixels(0, 0, m_bitmap->size().width(), m_bitmap->size().height(), supportsBGRAReadback ? GL_BGRA : GL_RGBA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, pixels.data());
+    if (!supportsBGRAReadback) {
+        // ShareableBitmap consumers expect BGRA; GLES guarantees RGBA/UNSIGNED_BYTE reads.
+        for (size_t offset = 0; offset < pixels.size(); offset += 4)
+            std::swap(pixels[offset], pixels[offset + 2]);
+    }
     RenderTargetShareableBuffer::didRenderFrame(WTF::move(damageRects));
 }
 
